# Secrets manifest (GPG vault)
#
# Format: <source-file><TAB><vault-filename>
#   - Relative paths are resolved against the repo root.
#   - Absolute paths are used as-is.
#   - `{DATA_ROOT}` is expanded to the data root (default: ~/homelab-data).
#
# The vault stores encrypted copies of files that must survive a reinstall:
# compose .env files, DuckDNS token, etc. The plaintext originals live in the
# repo / data dir and are excluded from git (see .gitignore).
#
# To add a secret: add a line here, then run secrets/encrypt.sh.
# To restore: run secrets/decrypt.sh (or the bootstrap does it).

compose/api/.env	api.env.gpg
compose/n8n/.env	n8n.env.gpg
{DATA_ROOT}/duckdns/duckdns.conf	duckdns.conf.gpg
